text.section:
Until July 1, 1991, the following single risk limits after deducting for reinsurance will apply:

No insurer having less than $2 million insurance in force shall insure any 1 risk for more than $10,000;


No insurer having more than $2 million but less than $5 million insurance in force shall insure any 1 risk for more than $12,000;


No insurer having more than $5 million but less than $10 million insurance in force shall insure any 1 risk for more than $20,000;


No insurer having more than $10 million insurance in force shall insure any 1 risk for a sum in excess of 15 cent(s) for each $100 insurance it has in force; and


An insurer may insure any one risk in larger sums than prescribed in this section if (i) the excess over such prescribed maximum is reinsured as authorized in this chapter or (ii) the excess may be increased by the extent of twenty-five percent of the surplus of the insurer as of the time the insurance is written.
